# Text Editors in Linux

Text editors are used to create and modify text files directly from the terminal.

Linux provides several text editors. The most common ones are:

- `nano` (beginner-friendly)
- `vim` (advanced)
- `vi` (basic version of vim)

---

## Nano (Beginner Friendly)

Nano is simple and easy to use.

### Open or Create a File

```bash
nano file.txt


